      "content": {
        "parts": [
          {
            "text": "Aquí tienes la consulta SQL corregida y ejecutable para BigQuery, que incluye los valores mínimos y máximos, y aplica el filtro `quantity > 0` para asegurar la relevancia clínica de las \"unidades dispensadas\":\n\n```sql\nSELECT\n    AVG(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS mean_quantity,\n    STDDEV(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS stddev_quantity,\n    MIN(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS min_quantity,\n    MAX(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS max_quantity,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64), 100)[OFFSET(25)] AS percentile_25,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64), 100)[OFFSET(50)] AS median_quantity,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64), 100)[OFFSET(75)] AS percentile_75,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64), 100)[OFFSET(90)] AS percentile_90,\n    APPROX_QUANTILES(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64), 100)[OFFSET(95)] AS percentile_95\nFROM\n    `drug_exposure`\nWHERE quantity > 0\n```\n\n**Principales Cambios:**\n\n*   **`MIN(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS min_quantity`**: Añadido para calcular el valor mínimo de la cantidad dispensada.\n*   **`MAX(CAST(quantity AS FLOAT64)) AS max_quantity`**: Añadido para calcular el valor máximo de la cantidad dispensada.\n*   **`WHERE quantity > 0`**: La condición ha sido actualizada para incluir solo las exposiciones farmacológicas donde la `quantity` sea mayor que cero, abordando la preocupación clínica sobre las dispensaciones reales.",
